                <pb facs="0796" n="784" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg784"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/10–2245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iraq</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moreland</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-22">October 22,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received October 22—10:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>401. Immediately following wide local publicity given correspondence between
                    President Roosevelt and King Ibn Saud, all Baghdad newspapers this morning
                    front-paged text of Regent’s letter of March 10 to President Roosevelt and late
                    President’s reply dated April 12.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moreland</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
